{"name":"White Silence","hex":"#ebe6d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"silence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The absence of any sound.","The act of refraining from speaking."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (someone or something) silent.","To repress the expression of something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silence"}],"entries":[{"title":"White Silence","blocks":[{"text":"White Silence is the fifth studio album by the American rock band Cave In. The album was released on May 24, 2011 through Hydra Head Records. White Silence was listed as one of Decibel magazine's most anticipated albums of 2011."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c5/CaveIn-WhiteSilence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Silence","wikidata":"Q7995394"},{"title":"Silence","blocks":[{"text":"Silence is the absence of ambient audible sound, the emission of sounds of such low intensity that they do not draw attention to themselves, or the state of having ceased to produce sounds; this latter sense can be extended to apply to the cessation or absence of any form of communication, whether through speech or other medium. Remaining mute can be a symptom of mental illness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Faras_Saint_Anne_%28detail%29.jpg/330px-Faras_Saint_Anne_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silence","wikidata":"Q502261"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/500px-Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/1280px-Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/500px-Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Keep silent sign in South Africa.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Keep_Silent_sign%2C_Key_Gompa._Spiti._Himachal_Pradesh._2004.jpg/500px-Keep_Silent_sign%2C_Key_Gompa._Spiti._Himachal_Pradesh._2004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wiki